Z||000002||BOILERMAKER||01-03-2001||06:11 PM||||I just keep the computer off.  Either that or I keep turning it on and off really fast so that the virus can't keep up with me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>How about this.  I keep a box of tissues on top of the monitor in case it catches a virus so it can blow its nose.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I use McAfee (spelling) and haven't had any problems, but then again I don't know many people who email me. Gosh, where do I come up with them?  I've tickled myself with this, so I must turn off my computer now.  LOL||||reg||1
Z||000003||Robert||01-03-2001||06:57 PM||||Norton has never let me down,<BR>.......pun intended  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||01-03-2001||07:24 PM||||To be honest, I don't use virus scanners and my computer has never been infected with a virus (well, not for the past 12 years anyway).<P>To protect yourself from viruses, just follow these simple rules:<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><LI> Never download software from sites that are not official download sites.<BR><LI>Never, ever open attachements in emails if you're not 100% sure what it is, or from whom it is.<BR><LI>This means that you should never use Outlook Express, since it will open attachements automatically in some instances.<BR><LI>This also means you shouldn't use Internet Explorer, since IE can start ActiveX programs by just visiting websites.<BR><LI>Always make sure Windows isn't hiding files and/or file-extensions.<BR><LI>Never install warez or copied software.<BR><LI>Best of all,run Linux instead of Windows  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><LI>Never boot your machine from anything but your harddisk, an official CD, or a self-created startup diskette.<BR><LI>Don't let anyone touch your PC but yourself.<BR></UL><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000005||LarryB||01-03-2001||10:41 PM||||Not Linux....FreeBSD or Solaris  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>If you're not ABSOLUTELY sure about an attachment don't open it, even if you know and trust the person who sent it.<P>Some of the more infamous viruses like Melissa and I LOVE YOU propogate by looking at the contents of the users contact list (Outlook is notorious for this) and sending a copy to those people.  The recipients would see who sent the attachment and then open it, figuring it was a legitimate executable sent by someone they knew.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87ECO5||01-04-2001||09:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by william_thorniii:<BR><B>Is it fair to assume that your home box has been inflicted?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It was.  We ended up "FDISKing" it in order to start from scratch.  It's back up now but missing a few critical files!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>We were running McAfee Viruscan ... but I guess the DAT files weren't recent enough.<P>We'll be playing this game a little differently from now on ...<P><B>BOILERMAKER</B> - you still on the cough medicine!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000007||rogergarrison||01-04-2001||09:54 AM||||I used to use Norton but got a virus anyway. Now I use McKafee. latest version can be set to scan every email, download before you even get to it. Also now Hotmail automaticly scans uploads and downloads for every email it passes.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||01-04-2001||10:12 AM||||I use FPROT. They are the best that I have tried. They usually have fixes and/or updates hours after a major new virus attack is started. They have an excellent website that explains in detail what the virus does and even how to get rid of some of the virus WITHOUT formatting the drive or anti-virus software.<BR>The only thing they do is virus' and encrypted data especially wireless. Also their programs don't eat a lot of memory like norton's. You can try-out the software for 30 days free. Once you purchase it you have free updates and upgrades! The link is included below.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.f-secure.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.f-secure.com/</A><P>This below link will get you to the virus list. Just select the letter the virus starts with and scroll down to it for the info. <A HREF="http://www.europe.f-secure.com/v-descs/a.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.europe.f-secure.com/v-descs/a.shtml</A> <BR> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-04-2001).]||||reg||1
